      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:57:26Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, RouteProcessor2 creation trace and historical runtime, Sushi's official post-mortem, and the commit-pinned reproduction. The exploit contract calls processRoute on 0x044b75f554b886a065b9567891e45c79542d7357 with an attacker-selected pool, then repeatedly calls the router's uniswapV3SwapCallback selector. The router directly executes the failure-bearing callback code and performs eight 100 WETH transferFrom calls against the approved wallet. The 11,861-byte direct runtime has hash 0xf9b86791ebacf39275775bec89c170be417ccc86a6b0d41bf020058f117337b8 both at deployment block 16980905 and immediately before the exploit; the exploit trace contains no delegatecall. The creation transaction is an EOA CREATE, and Sushi describes RouteProcessor2 as non-upgradeable, establishing deployment as the complete code-selection history and an age of 330,540 seconds."
    },
